  <Docs>
    <summary>Specifies the result of a service permission check.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>These are alternative result codes, not flags. <c>NsdManager.CheckPermissionForService</c> checks the stored service approval list for the caller. The result indicates whether Android remembers picker approval for access to that service without the local network permission; it is not a check of all permissions that can allow access.</para>
      <para>For apps that target Android 17 (API level 37) or later, the local network permission rules apply. A <c>Denied</c> result does not negate an independently granted <c>android.permission.ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK</c> permission: resolution and service information callback registration can still be permitted through that permission. A previous picker selection can be revoked; this check does not guarantee that the service is available.</para>
      <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/347fbd34b368d19f0d87e908ea101eed3601a731/framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/NsdManager.java">Android 17 source for NsdManager.checkPermissionForService and its result codes.</a></format></para>
      <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/347fbd34b368d19f0d87e908ea101eed3601a731/service-t/src/com/android/server/NsdService.java">Android 17 implementation of the stored service approval check and the independent local network permission check.</a></format></para>
    </remarks>
  </Docs>
